      "writtenOn": "2021-02-20T00:05:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I unfortunately don\u0027t have a DUT with a TCS3400 to experiment with.  \n\nDo you know whether TCS_I2C_STATUS_RGBC_VALID is set when using irq and ((status \u0026 TCS_I2C_STATUS_ALS_IRQ) \u0026\u0026 (status \u0026 TCS_I2C_STATUS_ALS_SATURATED)) is true?  If the sample data is actually set to 0xffff (TCS_SATURATION_LEVEL), the logic in this routine checking sample against TCS_SATURATION_LEVEL will deal with it correctly and assure a saturation level reading does not get sent outside of the driver, so I don\u0027t think any changes would be necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "15254df7_1ec48f94",
      "range": {
